  "notes": [
    "Converted from the old map.json/portals.json format by tools/map-converter. Every ring normal below was derived from the recorded rim points and oriented by the bisector of the flight path; see CourseConverter for why that rule and not the three simpler ones.",
    "spawn — read from the world\u0027s level.dat (SpawnX/SpawnY/SpawnZ), not derived.",
    "referenceTimeSeconds — PROVISIONAL seed of 60.0 s, not a measurement. It decides medal tiers only. Replace it with a real lap once someone has flown one.",
    "points — PROVISIONAL seed of 10 on every ring, carried over from the loader in the tree being replaced. The old data records no per-ring variation, so there is nothing here to preserve; a balancing pass edits this file.",
    "boostConfig.burnDurationTicks — PROVISIONAL seed of 30, derived rather than measured: Vanilla\u0027s rocket lifetime is 10 * flightDuration + random(6) + random(7), and this is that formula\u0027s deterministic core for flightDuration 3, the strongest rocket a player can craft. The random part is dropped on purpose — two identical boosts have to be worth the same in a race. The old file carried no burn at all. A balancing pass edits this number.",
    "boostConfig.cooldownTicks — carried from the old map.json\u0027s cooldownMs of 2000, converted once into the ticks a server counts in: 40. It is measured from the tick a boost STARTS, and has to stay longer than the burn — two rockets burning on one racer at once is a case the simulation\u0027s boolean boost input cannot express.",
    "guideLine.points — 16 point(s), carried from the old guides.json exactly as written. They are not rings: nothing is scored at one, and they exist only to pull the line off a straight ring-to-ring segment that would cut through terrain. orderIndex places a point between two rings, where ring i sits at i * 100; more than one guide between the same pair of rings is normal.",
    "guideLine.lookAheadRings — PROVISIONAL seed of 2, reasoned rather than flown: the line is drawn from the ring a racer is heading for to 2 ring(s) past it, which on this course is a few seconds of flight. Drawing the whole course at once tells a racer nothing about which strand is next.",
    "guideLine.particleSpacing — PROVISIONAL seed of 1.0 block(s) between particles, the value the tree being replaced used for the same partial-line mode. Halving it doubles what one racer\u0027s stretch costs to send every refresh.",
    "This file is data, not code: edit the seeds above here rather than in the server.",
    "35 rings, indexed 0..34."
  ]
}
